# The baselines are compared byte for byte against what rnx2rtkp actually
# writes, and .pos uses CRLF line endings.  The repository root sets
# `* text=auto`, which normalises those CRLFs to LF on commit -- a fresh clone
# would then hold a baseline that differs from the program's real output and
# the G1 gate would fail for a reason that has nothing to do with the code.
#
# Observed before this rule existed: solution.pos was stored as 15824 bytes
# instead of 15941, with 117 CR bytes silently removed.
#
# Store them exactly as generated.
datasets/**/baseline/solution.pos  -text
datasets/**/baseline/solution.stat -text
